# Engineering standards

## Security

- Never trust `X-Tenant-Id` as authorization; derive tenant from authenticated identity.
- Least privilege; secrets in a secrets manager; no credentials in git or logs.
- Parameterized SQL; encryption in transit and at rest; auditable admin actions.

## Reliability

- Health vs readiness; timeouts; bounded retries; idempotent ops; graceful shutdown.
- Tested backups/restore; rollback procedures; failure isolation.

## Observability

- Structured JSON logs; correlation/trace IDs; tenant-aware telemetry with controlled cardinality.
- Actionable alerts; measurable SLOs; documented error budgets.

## Infrastructure / app

- Reusable IaC; env separation; private DB networking; proportional architecture (no K8s for show).
- Small components; positive and negative tests; pinned dependencies.
